+# Isolated result-contract controls
+
+result.schema.json and provenance.schema.json are the durable approved schema snapshots, promoted from the Issue 6 planning contract by parent message msg_e68cb7319918. The minimal Python subset reader is test-only, dependency-free and resolves solely from this fixture directory, including after task archive.
+
+Parent clarification msg_a524a52bec20 / msg_a3e0e00db0ed permits artifact.bytes >= 0 structurally. Semantically a zero-byte artifact is permitted only as an immutable-input source snapshot bound in immutableInputs, or the exact already validated identity reused in restore.inputs/build.inputs. The snapshot retains original bytes and SHA; an empty artifact cannot satisfy result/report evidence, manifest, required log, binary identity or coverage. Tests exercise this exception through the real shared dotnet body with fake native execution; generated example=true artifacts are rejected by production mode.
+
+Run powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/tests/test-gate-result-contract.tests.ps1 for the full isolated suite. No real dotnet build, Unity, services, network, soak or performance workload is launched. SkipRunnerIntegration is a focused subset and cannot establish full-suite acceptance. Unique ignored local/Artifacts roots retain original failures and command/source/tool receipts.
+
+Slice B1 binds resultType/kind/name and leaf shape to the configured invocation. The current result schema additionally constrains gate versus leaf shape; the declared Python keyword subset now includes allOf/maxItems. Invocation binding remains a production semantic check, not a schema-only claim.
+
+b1-controls.ps1 exercises all eleven bounded adapters' real bodies. body-source-adapter.ps1 supplies a narrow synthetic source scope, always example=true; the surrounding harness captures and checks the complete actual repository before/after. sample-executor.ps1 fakes every dotnet evaluation/restore/build/run and intercepts at entry before work. deterministic-child-executor.ps1 allows only the four deterministic PowerShell bodies used by the two assertion harnesses; those PowerShell child processes are real and their command/native exit/logs are retained. It blocks .NET/services and unknown children. No fake early-return producer implementation substitutes for the body.
+
+Report chains serialize explicit predecessor role/result/artifact hashes. Producer input manifests bind original archived bytes (including a legitimate empty input) and recheck current inputs; only explicitly bound immutable-input snapshots permit zero bytes. All result/report/raw/binary artifacts remain nonempty. Script audit criteria remain tests=null (N/A), while assertion harnesses count raw assertion entries. sample log display names may contain spaces; serialized evidence uses safe generated IDs and retains a name map.
+
+Default UPM and hero audit failures are preserved as actual failures; isolated positives specify known-valid packages or a separate policy fixture. These controls do not fix or grant acceptance to the current repository's dependency/CI policy gaps. Four service adapters remain B2b; clean-source real runtime-contracts remains C work.
+
+tools/test-gates.json explicitly declares evidenceType for the fourteen adapted producers and sourceStep/role edges for report predecessors, plus the sample/Unity project contracts and sample build predecessor. Runner consumes these declarations; missing, unsupported or contradictory evidence and missing/ambiguous/mismatched predecessors fail before producer execution. Known adapter identity uses its resolved repository path, so path aliases cannot bypass the declaration requirement. Controls exercise the production runner with the real three-body report chain, configured type mutations and an exit0 producer without a receipt. Default evidence roots use a short i6 UUID prefix to keep Windows PowerShell paths within its host limits; artifacts remain isolated and retained.
+
+## B2a contracts and prerequisites
+
+The two benchmark wrappers now execute their actual bodies through entry-level fake native executors in controls. Gate context records an explicit restore/build and runs the bound binary with --no-build/--no-restore; standalone CLI retains its original implicit dotnet run build and native exit. Runtime report acceptance completes measurement coverage only. AOI validates the existing smoke/full case matrix and unchanged thresholds; native threshold exit2 is Failed1 with native2 retained. Reports are bound to invocation UUIDs, source/config, evaluated project/configuration/TFM, sample/outcome semantics and archived binary identity. Missing, malformed, stale, wrong-scope and contradictory reports fail. Fixtures do not benchmark.
+
+coverageDimensions in tools/test-gates.json supplies concrete expected configuration, TFM, host, policy and scope; the pure resolver appends those dimensions and a deterministic hash of configured arguments to declarations. It never probes an uninvoked host or guesses coverage from result names. Raw receipts cannot contain unresolved templates. Actual evaluated TFM/configuration, command filters and configured argument bindings must match before completion. The four Server/Orleans adapters still fail closed pending B2b; their concrete net10.0 declarations grant no completed service coverage.
+
+Installed Unity mirror requires explicit UnityBuildProofPath in a bound gate invocation. The proof schema is unity-build-proof.schema.json (abilitykit.unity-build-proof.v1): current run/config/source fingerprint before/after, prior successful editor compilation command/native exit/times/log, exact Unity version and editor identity, and before/after plus archived/current identity for the required project assemblies. Existing DLL bytes, a later hash capture or an installation path alone are not build proof. Absent proof is Blocked/MissingUnityProjectBinaryProvenance; malformed or mismatched proof is Failed. Optional conversion remains limited to exact MissingUnityInstallation. Standalone mirror reports Blocked2 once installation/project binaries exist because it has no bound current-run build context. This slice provides no production Unity compilation/proof exporter and does not claim the local installation or Library binaries are validated. A separately authorized, instrumented current-source Unity compile must supply the full proof before actual mirror/Unity acceptance can be attempted.
+
+Unity EditMode/PlayMode require declared assembly names, the same prerequisite build proof, current raw NUnit, reconciled executed counts and loaded assembly paths, and a host/filter/policy/report binding. An occupied project's UnityLockfile is Blocked/UnityProjectInUse and is never removed. Execute-method requires resultsFile and a method that consumes -abilityKitResultContext/-abilityKitResultFile and writes the exact abilitykit.unity-execute-method.v1 completion schema in unity-execute-method.schema.json. It is N/A for tests. There is currently no configured production execute-method producer; lack of completion/provenance cannot pass. unity-executor.ps1 exercises each actual runner path with only synthetic owned bytes and intercepted native operations; example=true proof/results cannot establish production acceptance.
+
+Frozen-B1 coordinator findings are regression controls: serialized dictionary/object binding IDs stay nonempty through nested aggregation; canonical status/kind/root enums are case exact; native stdout/stderr is captured as raw stream text without parent ErrorRecord formatting. Original coordinator evidence remains read-only. ControlFilter and SkipRunnerIntegration declare subsets and cannot set fullControlSuiteAccepted; total and executed are recorded separately. All earlier local b2f/b2u failures and raw invocation logs are retained.
